AIHub — Alembic Database Migrations
=====================================

Common commands (run from the backend/ directory):

  Create a new migration (auto-detect changes):
    alembic revision --autogenerate -m "description of change"

  Apply all pending migrations:
    alembic upgrade head

  Rollback one migration:
    alembic downgrade -1

  Rollback to a specific revision:
    alembic downgrade <revision_id>

  Show current revision:
    alembic current

  Show migration history:
    alembic history --verbose

  Show pending migrations:
    alembic history -r current:head

Rules:
  - Never edit a migration file after it has been applied to any environment.
  - Always review autogenerated migrations before applying them.
  - The migrations/versions/ directory is version-controlled.
  - Never delete migration files — use downgrade scripts instead.
